(Section 3: Bearing Fault Progression Stages and Maintenance Actions) Tj T*
(Stage 1 \(Subsurface micro-spalling\): ultrasonic/spike energy in 20 to 60 kHz band;) Tj T*
(normal time-domain RMS and kurtosis near 3.0. Action: continue normal monitoring.) Tj T*
(Stage 2 \(Incipient raceway spall\): ringing of bearing/housing natural frequencies) Tj T*
(\(typically 1.5 to 5 kHz\) modulated at BPFO, BPFI, or BSF; kurtosis rises above 4.0) Tj T*
(and crest factor exceeds 5.0. Action: check lubrication and shorten inspection interval) Tj T*
(to 2 weeks.) Tj T*
(Stage 3 \(Discrete fault harmonics in baseband FFT\): fundamental BPFO/BPFI/BSF and) Tj T*
(harmonics \(1x, 2x, 3x\) with sidebands spaced at shaft speed \(BPFI\) or FTF \(BSF\)) Tj T*
(become visible in the baseband FFT spectrum. Action: schedule bearing replacement) Tj T*
(within the next planned maintenance window and perform lubricant wear debris analysis.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
